From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 11:09:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] slimbus: stream: check that each port connects to its channel

slim_stream_prepare() discards the return of
slim_connect_port_channel(), so a CONNECT_SOURCE or CONNECT_SINK that
the bus rejects is not reported and not unwound. The port is left
allocated and marked SLIM_PORT_UNCONFIGURED but not bound to any
channel, while slim_stream_prepare() returns success and every layer
above it -- DAPM, the AFE port, the DSP session -- goes on to start
cleanly.

On capture the result is a stream that runs with correct timing and
delivers one repeated sample value, with nothing in any log to say why.

Check the return, unwind the ports already connected, and hand the error
back so the caller can fail where the fault is.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/slimbus/stream.c | 15 +++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/slimbus/stream.c b/drivers/slimbus/stream.c
index e2316be83c04..630f0887a9d7 100644
--- a/drivers/slimbus/stream.c
+++ b/drivers/slimbus/stream.c
@@ -206,7 +206,7 @@ int slim_stream_prepare(struct slim_stream_runtime *rt,
 {
 	struct slim_controller *ctrl = rt->dev->ctrl;
 	struct slim_port *port;
-	int num_ports, i, port_id, prrate;
+	int num_ports, i, port_id, prrate, ret;
 
 	if (rt->ports) {
 		dev_err(&rt->dev->dev, "Stream already Prepared\n");
@@ -263,7 +263,18 @@ int slim_stream_prepare(struct slim_stream_runtime *rt,
 		else
 			port->direction = SLIM_PORT_SOURCE;
 
-		slim_connect_port_channel(rt, port);
+		ret = slim_connect_port_channel(rt, port);
+		if (ret) {
+			dev_err(&rt->dev->dev,
+				"Failed to connect port %d to channel %d: %d\n",
+				port->id, port->ch.id, ret);
+			while (i--)
+				slim_disconnect_port(rt, &rt->ports[i]);
+			kfree(rt->ports);
+			rt->ports = NULL;
+			rt->num_ports = 0;
+			return ret;
+		}
 		i++;
 	}
 
